Package: linux-xiaomi-marble
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, kmod, linux-base
Recommends: firmware-xiaomi-marble
Description: Linux kernel for Xiaomi Redmi Note 12 Turbo (marble)
 Mainline Linux 7.2.8 kernel with the marble (Poco F5 / Redmi Note 12 Turbo,
 SM7475), based on iLtanaka's device enablement. LazyBonesLZY ported the
 front and macro cameras, including Shandorman's S5K3P9 driver. The OV64B40
 main camera driver and board wiring come from dianqk.
 .
 Built with LLVM/ThinLTO and ccache. Ships the uncompressed kernel Image
 (as vmlinuz-<ver>), the device tree, and kernel modules including
 v4l2loopback for V4L2 camera applications. No initramfs is generated
 (no-initramfs direct boot, the path verified by the
 original port); the postinst requires /boot/efi to be a vfat ESP
 (PARTLABEL=esp or filesystem LABEL=ESP), then syncs vmlinuz + DTB. It creates
 /extlinux/extlinux.conf only on first installation and preserves it on
 upgrades; an upgrade with no boot entry fails before the kernel and DTB are
 replaced.
 .
 Local deviations from the author's reference config live in the kconfig
 fragment extra-kernel.config, merged on top at build time.
